WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.824
"How to Improve Your Heart Rate Variability"

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.960
Everyone feel for your pulse.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.880
Hold out your hand, thumb up,

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.360
and feel for the knobby bone
at the top of your wrist.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.140
Okay, now,
slide your hand down

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.360
and across the front
of your wrist.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.280
Feel those, like,
strands of spaghetti?

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.720
Those are the tendons
in your wrist.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.360
If you press lightly
between the knobby bone

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.800
and that first tendon,
you should feel your pulse.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.280
Got it?

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.480
Okay,
now what we're going to do

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.880
is feel what happens
to our pulse

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.680
when we take a deep breath.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.080
We're going to try it twice.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.080
Try to feel what happens
to your pulse when you inhale

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.280
and when you exhale.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.100
All right, here we go,
slow inhale.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.640
(inhales)

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.940
Slow exhale.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.680
(exhales)

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.440
One more time.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.840
In.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:00:59.920
Out.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.920
What happened when you
breathed in and breathed out?

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.520
You should have felt your pulse
speed up when you inhaled

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.240
and slow down
when you exhaled.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:14.160
That's called
heart rate variability,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.720
a measure of the control

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.640
our vagus nerve has
over our heart.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.080
And it's a good thing.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.520
A healthy heart
is not a metronome.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.320
Low heart rate variability
predicts greater risk

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:29.280
of heart disease and death
from several causes.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.440
High-risk patients with
low variability in heart rate

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.600
have twice the risk
of dying prematurely.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.640
Is there anything we can do

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.320
to positively impact
heart rate variability?

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.080
Voluntary slow breathing,
at about six breaths per minute,

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.480
is a technique that's been used
for thousands of years

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.520
as an essential part

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.920
of many meditative
and relaxation practices.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:56.320
It can benefit several heart
rate variability parameters,

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.840
offering a low-tech,
low-cost technique.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.280
Speaking of low-tech, low-cost:
What about exercise?

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.400
Aerobic training
at least twice a week

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.800
positively influences
heart nerve control.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.080
What about what we eat?

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.040
Those eating plant-based diets

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.680
have better
overall heart rate variability.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.040
Vegetarians, for example,

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.720
don't tend to have only
better blood pressure,

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.520
cholesterol, triglycerides,
and blood sugars,

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.840
they also have
better heart rate variability.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.960
The vagus nerve toning effects
of plant-based diets

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.640
may help explain part of
their cardioprotective effect.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.640
Any plants in particular?

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.800
While no significant association
was seen

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.480
between heart rate
variability measures

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.520
and the intake of fruits
and vegetables in general,

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.480
the consumption
of green leafy vegetables

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.720
seems to stand out,

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:49.800
perhaps helping to explain

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.200
why eating just a half serving
of greens a day

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.920
may cut our risk
of having a heart attack

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.200
by up to 67 percent!

